This mutation changes how a MOVE is scored. A step now earns more the further it closes the gap to the goals, and it is penalised when it ends next to an enemy champion. `progress` is unchanged. The enemy-adjacency check is the only added engine call, so it is the main fuel cost.

```python
@gene("s1", "value of doing this option now: moves scale with progress, penalised next to enemy champions", parents=["s1"])
def score(o: Option) -> Num:
    if o.kind == PICK:
        return 1
    if o.kind == BUY:
        return 100 if o.item == 6 else 0
    if o.kind == RECALL:
        return 90 if me().health_frac < 0.35 else 0
    if o.kind == ATTACK:
        if o.unit.is_champion:
            return 80
        return 60 if gems() == 0 else 0
    if o.kind == TRIBUTE:
        return 70
    if o.kind == MOVE:
        p = progress(o.tile)
        if p <= 0:
            return 0
        risk = count(1 for u in enemies() if u.is_champion and dist(u.pos, o.tile) <= 2)
        return 40 + 10 * p - 30 * risk
    return 0
```

This mutation makes `progress` a safety-weighted step. A step still earns the distance gained toward the goals, but each enemy within 3 tiles of the destination costs 3 points. The MOVE score's `progress(o.tile) > 0` gate stays as is, so a step that gains ground but walks into enemy reach is no longer valued as highly. The cost is one extra scan of `enemies()` per candidate step; I kept it direct rather than adding a per-turn keep to avoid stale-set bugs.

```python
@gene("s4", "distance gained toward goals minus a penalty for enemies near the destination", parents=["s4"])
def progress(t: Tile) -> Num:
    return at(goal_field(), me().pos) - at(goal_field(), t) - 3 * count(1 for u in enemies() if dist(u.pos, t) <= 3)
```

This mutation makes the goal field route around enemy champions. I used `field_avoid` with the enemy tiles as walls (minus the goals themselves, so goal tiles stay reachable) and a small local stop set around me, so the search ends early and stays cheap.

```python
@gene("s3", "distance field to the goals, routing around enemy champions", parents=["s3"])
def goal_field() -> Field:
    return field_avoid(goals(), enemy_tiles() - goals(), near(me().pos, 3))
```

```python
@gene("s4", "how much closer a step brings me to the goals, enemy-avoiding field", parents=["s4"])
def progress(t: Tile) -> Num:
    return at(goal_field(), me().pos) - at(goal_field(), t)
```

This mutation changes `goal_field` to use `field_avoid`, so the distance search stops once it reaches my immediate neighbourhood instead of flooding the whole map. Walls are unchanged. The cost is that tiles beyond that layer read as unreachable, so `progress` is only accurate for steps near me, which is all it compares.

```python
@gene("s3", "distance field to the goals, search stopped near me (cheaper)", parents=["s3"])
def goal_field() -> Field:
    return field_avoid(goals(), walls(), near(me().pos, 1))
```

```python
@gene("s4", "how much closer a step brings me to the goals", parents=["s4"])
def progress(t: Tile) -> Num:
    return at(goal_field(), me().pos) - at(goal_field(), t)
```

This mutation caches the goal field once per turn instead of rebuilding it on every pass of the loop. `goal_field()` now returns a keep that `update()` fills, so `progress` reads the same distances at a fraction of the fuel. Routing is unchanged, apart from goals that could shift within a single turn.

```python
GOAL_FIELD: Field = None

@gene("s5", "goal distance field cached once per turn", parents=["s3"])
def goal_field() -> Field:
    return GOAL_FIELD

@gene("s6", "compute the goal field once at the start of each turn", parents=["s3"])
def update() -> None:
    GOAL_FIELD = field(goals())
```

This mutation caches the goal distance field once per turn instead of recomputing it on every pass of the loop, which cuts fuel. `goal_field` now returns the cached keep. The field is built from `goals()` at turn start, so it can be slightly stale after a move within the turn.

```python
GOAL_FIELD: Field = None

@gene("s5", "goal distance field cached once per turn (update), returned cheaply on each pass", parents=["s3"])
def goal_field() -> Field:
    return GOAL_FIELD

@gene("s6", "per-turn refresh of the cached goal distance field", parents=["s3"])
def update() -> None:
    GOAL_FIELD = field(goals())
```

This mutation changes only `cast_value`. It makes shields and heals fire earlier and harder when a close enemy threatens us, lets dashes trigger on real progress gain, and keeps damage on awake camps useful even while carrying gems.

```python
@gene('Z38a', 'value of casting an ability option: shield/heal when threatened, dash for real progress, damage awake camps even when carrying', parents=['s1'])
def cast_value(o: Option) -> Num:
    k = slot_kind(o.slot)
    if k == AB_DAMAGE or k == AB_AOE or k == AB_CC:
        if exists(o.unit):
            if o.unit.is_enemy and o.unit.is_champion:
                return 85
            if o.unit.is_camp:
                if gems() == 0:
                    return 65
                if is_awake(o.unit):
                    return 40
        return 0
    if k == AB_SHIELD or k == AB_HEAL:
        near = count(dist(u.pos, me().pos) <= 3 for u in enemies())
        if me().health_frac < 0.6 and near > 0:
            return 88
        if me().health_frac < 0.8 and near > 1:
            return 70
        return 0
    if k == AB_DASH:
        if valid(o.tile):
            gain = progress(me().pos) - progress(o.tile)
            if gain > 2:
                return 60
        return 0
    return 0
```
